# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
**/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
**/.next/
# The gateway settings page's static export: build output, rebuilt by its app setup step.
**/out-build/
/out/
**/out/

# production
/build
**/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
.docker-host-dev/
.docker-host-dev-demo/
.docker-host-dev-user/
.docker-host-prod-demo/

# local Docker Host runtime state
/.docker-host-dev/
/.docker-host-dev-demo/
/.hosty-dev*/

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# dotnet
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Built SDK package output (publish-time artifact, never committed)
packages/*/dist/

# Next.js 16.3.4+ writes an AGENTS.md (a managed "nextjs-agent-rules" block) and a CLAUDE.md
# (`@AGENTS.md`) into every app directory on `next dev`, and re-creates them on the next run — there
# is no switch. Not committed: they are vendor-generated, identical across apps, and would dirty the
# tree on every Next bump. Scoped to apps/ so the repository's own root AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md stay
# tracked. The files still exist locally and agents working inside an app directory still read them.
apps/*/AGENTS.md
apps/*/CLAUDE.md
